issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- tested in v4.4.stable.official [4c311cbee]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7242) - AMD Ryzen 7 3800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn 4.4, reflection probes seem to no longer take SDFGI into account when getting ambient light from environment, leading to very poor blending and inaccurate reflections.\n\n| 4.3 | 4.4 |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/da5da02a-63d8-4b02-8d0a-102ac9148fb3) no reflection probe | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f44ef367-bb91-4721-a234-0cf8417f3bb1) no reflection probe |\n| ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4649aba6-5730-4da4-b4df-8f24f113e3de) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/16afbcf8-5d1d-416b-b772-5ba4c6236ec2) |\n| ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/57670176-d884-48ea-9c90-065d5968108e) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c5989955-12b7-40d3-9051-71ec198d8dc3) |\n| ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dcbd376d-a2f4-442e-a135-f2a5e7da0532) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3a4c3d42-290e-43db-a3c4-222bf670cb0f) |\n| ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f5a190c4-488a-44df-a353-ae98fc9fe3da) reflection probe light blends into sdfgi light seamlessly | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fcad9332-5b37-45b6-89d3-a5be44570ce1) sharp transition from reflection probe to sdfgi (default setting, 1 unit blending) |\n\nSidenote, it seems like roughness no longer means the same thing as it did before the update.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nPut a reflection probe into SDFGI environment in 4.4\n\